The simple show explains the carbon footprint.

602
00:33:43,796 --> 00:33:50,516
This is you. You've probably been hearing a lot about climate change and how you should reduce your carbon footprint.

603
00:33:51,956 --> 00:33:59,236
But what is that exactly? Just like an actual footprint, it's a mark you leave upon the environment.

604
00:33:59,236 --> 00:34:12,596
No, not with your shoes, but with every action that releases carbons. Those are the harmful gases, such as CO2, which are pumped out by burning fossil fuels like oil or gas.

605
00:34:13,476 --> 00:34:23,316
The more fuel you use, the bigger your footprint will be. You may think that by driving your car, the only carbons you release come from the engine, but no.

606
00:34:23,316 --> 00:34:38,356
Consider the carbons that are emitted just to get fuel into the tank. From the energy needed to extract the oil from underground, the pollution caused by transportation and refinement, to the final delivery to your local petrol station.

607
00:34:39,076 --> 00:34:44,916
Not to mention the CO2 released by manufacturing your car in the first place. More than you thought, huh?

608
00:34:44,916 --> 00:34:51,956
So unless you live in a cave, you and everything you own has its own carbon footprint.

